Z||000000||Fatal Error||08-08-2001||07:36 PM||||Hey guys,<BR>I've got this co-worker who has a 84 rabbit with a 91 2.0L 16v out of a Jetta GLI talking smack. The engine is totally stock except he had new cams and a head job done (port, polish) that kinda thing. The interior of the car has been gutted and he has some sparco racing seats in it. He is claiming that he spanks fieros and is doing low 13s in the 1/4???? hmmm That engine cannot be putting out much over 100hp maybe 120 to 130 at best. I might just be dumb, but it doesn't seem right. What do you guys think? Thanks!<P>-Fatal||||reg||1
Z||000001||RacinRob||08-08-2001||08:12 PM||||well the engine makes 134 hp stock give him 16 hp for the mods and that is 150 a gutted rabbit really can't be that heavy, so I guess he has a good chance||||reg||1
Z||000002||Eric_PA||08-08-2001||08:27 PM||||I have a friend that is into VW's and he has a 2.0 16V in a schirocco (spelling?) many mads to it and he runs high 14's. He claims he is at 170HP. There are many mods for that engine. It sounds like if he can drive it, that he can take a stock Fiero. I have been in many HE$$ rides with rabbits...they handle very well for an econo box. With a 16V engine they are quick.<P>Eric||||reg||12
Z||000003||Fatal Error||08-08-2001||08:55 PM||||Even at 150hp .. even if he beat a v6 fiero .. I wouldn't classify it as a spanking. Also I was more concerned about the 1/4 times. I seriously doubt he is running low 13s. Just wanted some clarification. Thanks guys!<P>-Fatal||||reg||12
